    "id": "train-327",
    "question": "It takes 15 mink skins to make a coat. Andy buys 30 minks and each mink has 6 babies, but half the total minks are set free by activists. How many coats can he make?",
    "gold": "7",
    "answer": "First find the total number of baby minks: 30 minks * 6 babies/mink = <<30*6=180>>180 minks\nAdd this to the number of adult minks: 180 minks + 30 minks = <<180+30=210>>210 minks\nThen divide this number in half to find how many aren't set free: 210 minks / 2 = <<210/2=105>>105 minks\nThen divide the remaining number of minks by the number of minks per coat to find the number of coats: 105 minks / 15 minks/coat = <<105/15=7>>7 coats\n#### 7"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many coats Andy can make, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of minks Andy has after the babies are born.\n2. Determine how many minks are left after half of them are set free.\n3. Calculate how many coats can be made with the remaining minks.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of minks Andy has after the babies are born.\nAndy buys 30 minks and each mink has 6 babies. Therefore, the total number of babies is:\n\\[ 30 \\times 6 = 180 \\]\nSo, the total number of minks Andy has is:\n\\[ 30 + 180 = 210 \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine how many minks are left after half of them are set free.\nHalf of the total minks are set free, so the number of minks left is:\n\\[ \\frac{210}{2} = 105 \\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate how many coats can be made with the remaining minks.\nIt takes 15 mink skins to make one coat. Therefore, the number of coats Andy can make is:\n\\[ \\frac{105}{15} = 7 \\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{7} \\]",
